    {
      "id": 49288,
      "name": "Koga",
      "username": "Koga",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-12-13T00:17:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So does this overwrite&nbsp;the previous official ruling in the Silver Gulch thread? Here's a few quotes from that thread. Edited to avoid revealing too much about the environment.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If I'm not mistaken, I'm pretty sure that it was stated a discard doesn't cause an environment/villain deck resuffle, the discard is simply cancelled. Also, a trash is not resuffled unless a card is to be played (environment/villain) or a card is to be drawn (hero). A trash is not to be resuffled simply because the deck is empty. So, even if there were only one or two cards left when played, it would simply put all the cards in the trash.</p>\n<p>But, since I've been told that discarding doesn't cause a resuffle, this isn't an issue.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Koga\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/48/2058_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Koga:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I've always played that discarding can cause a reshuffle. Haven't seen any official ruling that says you don't reshuffle if you need to discard and there is nothing left in the deck. With this environment depending on the answer, would be nice to get an official ruling.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Christopher\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/48/1851_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Christopher:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You would only reshuffle when a card needs to be played and the deck is empty. That said, if people play it \"wrong\", they'll reshuffle and then discard, so that's not too huge of an issue.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>",
      "post_number": 16,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:22:41.189Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 6896,
      "topic_slug": "recycle-the-environment-and-villain-trash",
      "display_username": "Koga",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "So does this overwrite&nbsp;the previous official ruling in the Silver Gulch thread? Here&#39;s a few quotes from that thread. Edited to avoid revealing too much about the environment.\n\n[quote=\"TheJayMann\"]\n\nIf I&#39;m not mistaken, I&#39;m pretty sure that it was stated a discard doesn&#39;t cause an environment/villain deck resuffle, the discard is simply cancelled. Also, a trash is not resuffled unless a card is to be played (environment/villain) or a card is to be drawn (hero). A trash is not to be resuffled simply because the deck is empty. So, even if there were only one or two cards left when played, it would simply put all the cards in the trash.\n\nBut, since I&#39;ve been told that discarding doesn&#39;t cause a resuffle, this isn&#39;t an issue.\n\n[/quote]\n\n[quote=\"Koga\"]\n\nI&#39;ve always played that discarding can cause a reshuffle. Haven&#39;t seen any official ruling that says you don&#39;t reshuffle if you need to discard and there is nothing left in the deck. With this environment depending on the answer, would be nice to get an official ruling.\n\n[/quote]\n\n[quote=\"Christopher\"]\n\nYou would only reshuffle when a card needs to be played and the deck is empty. That said, if people play it &quot;wrong&quot;, they&#39;ll reshuffle and then discard, so that&#39;s not too huge of an issue.\n\n[/quote]\n\n",
